`SurveyFlow` has stages `draft`, `review`, and `sent`, starts at `draft`, and stores required answers `name` and `region`. `setAnswer` is allowed only in draft, trims its value, and stores it. `next()` from draft may proceed only when both stored answers are non-blank; otherwise it throws `Error("Incomplete survey")`. From review, `next()` moves to sent and invokes every subscribed listener once with a fresh answer object in subscription order. Calling `next()` when sent is a no-op. `previous()` moves review to draft and otherwise does nothing. `reset()` returns to draft and clears answers without removing listeners. `subscribe` returns an idempotent unsubscribe function. Listener mutation of its argument must not affect stored state or other listeners. `snapshot()` returns a defensive copy.

